From b3cb4a1e67ec478939d2c48a6a0563c3c9500fe2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lokitha Thangavel <lthangav@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 3 Dec 2025 11:18:07 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] QSDK:CP:HOSTAPD: Fix double free of BSS object name

In hostapd_ubus_free_bss(struct hostapd_data), the code unconditionally
calls free(name)

After the first teardown, obj->name still points to freed memory.
If the function is invoked again (e.g., repeated BSS teardown paths,
error-retry, or cleanup sequences), the same pointer is freed a
second time, causing a double free.

Guard the free(name) with a null check and explicitly set
obj->name = NULL after freeing. This eliminates a crash due to
heap corruption/double free.

Patch-dependency: none

Signed-off-by: Lokitha Thangavel <lthangav@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 src/ap/ubus.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ap/ubus.c b/src/ap/ubus.c
index 266622c..622b0ae 100644
--- a/src/ap/ubus.c
+++ b/src/ap/ubus.c
@@ -1682,7 +1682,10 @@ void hostapd_ubus_free_bss(struct hostapd_data *hapd)
 	ubus_remove_object(ctx, obj);
 	hostapd_ubus_ref_dec();
 
-	free(name);
+	if(name) {
+		free(name);
+		obj->name = NULL;
+	}
 }
 
 static void
